❗️  The Armed Forces of the Russian Federation, in response to terrorist attacks launched by the Kiev regime against civilian infrastructure on the territory of the Russian Federation, carried out a massive strike with long-range air-, ground-, and sea-based high-precision weapons and attack drones, which hit enterprises of the defence industry and fuel and power facilities in Kiev and Kiev region, as well as infrastructure of military airfields in Dnepropetrovsk, Poltava, Cherkassy, Chernigov, and Kiev regions.

The following targets were hit in Kiev:

▪️  The LLC RADIONICS unit and component manufacturing enterprise, which is a key scientific and production base that manufactures Flamingo long-range ground-based cruise missile control systems, Fire Point-7,-9 operational-tactical missiles, Neptune-MD guided missiles, and Klon project surface-to-air guided missiles. Also, the enterprise's products have a direct impact on the combat capabilities of the Ukrainian Air Force and its ability to counter air defence systems;

▪️  the electronic assembly plant (Athlon Avia LLC Scientific Production Company). One of the Ukrainian key defence industry enterprises providing the AFU with An-196 Lyuty long-range unmanned aerial vehicles, Magura UA attack UAVs, as well as other types of UAVs and loitering munitions;

▪️  the Antonov Serial Production Plant, which is the main production base in Ukraine that develops and manufactures manned military aircraft, as well as assembles and modernises An-196 Lyuty long-range unmanned aerial vehicles;

▪️  the missile unit and component plant (JSC Kiev Radio Plant, LLC TRIMEN-UKRAINE), which is a leading enterprise that modernises sighting systems for all types of tanks and armoured vehicles manufactured in Ukraine, produces optical sightings and guidance devices for armoured vehicles, and components for almost all reconnaissance and attack UAVs. In addition, the enterprise's integrated circuitry, microassembly components for SAM systems, electronic warfare systems, and aviation equipment directly affect the combat capabilities of these systems, which are in the service of the Armed Forces of Ukraine;

▪️  the KIEV-25 industrial enterprise (PV GROUP UKRAINE), which manufactures and stores software and hardware of the Lima electronic warfare system for the GNSS spoofing in high-precision fire engagement systems;

▪️  the MLP-CHAIKA transport and logistics centre, which is used to store long-range unmanned aerial vehicles, combat units and ammunition, as well as various exported components and hardware;

▪️  the KIEV-3 POL depot (LLC Grand-Terminal) supplying diesel fuel from the Novograd-Volynsky pipeline operation control station to military units of the Kiev garrison, including air defence units. In addition, diesel fuel from this depot is sent to the AFU units in the combat zone;

▪️ gas distribution stations in Kiev and Kiev region, which support the work of defence enterprises of the AFU. 

🔹 Russian Defence Ministry

